        "Set up the volume of revolution integral from $x = 0$ to $x = 1$:\n$$V = \\pi \\int_0^1 \\left[ (x + 1)^4 + 2(x + 1) + (x + 1)^{-2} \\right]\\,dx$$",
        "Integrate using the reverse chain rule:\n$$V = \\pi \\left[ \\frac{(x + 1)^5}{5} + (x + 1)^2 - (x + 1)^{-1} \\right]_0^1$$",
        "Evaluate between the limits $x = 0$ and $x = 1$:\n$$\\text{At } x = 1: \\quad \\frac{2^5}{5} + 2^2 - \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{32}{5} + 4 - \\frac{1}{2} = 6.4 + 4 - 0.5 = 9.9$$\n$$\\text{At } x = 0: \\quad \\frac{1^5}{5} + 1^2 - 1 = \\frac{1}{5} + 1 - 1 = 0.2$$\n$$V = \\pi(9.9 - 0.2) = 9.7\\pi \\quad (\\text{or } \\approx 30.5)$$"
